  "manual": {
    "notes": [
      "PARENTAGE IS UNSUPPORTED LEGEND (research 2026-07-03): tree names her parents as \"General William Charles Howe Taylor\" and \"Charlotte Ann MacDonald,\" but New Brunswick genealogists who have researched this well-documented \"Mother of Tabusintac\" figure state flatly there is no record of a General by that name in British or North American military/vital records. The one primary document located, her 1755 Holborn Lying-In Hospital christening record, instead names her parents as Charles Taylor, a Kensington gardener, and his wife Ann Taylor; treat the \"General\" parentage as family legend, not fact. New finding: per charlottetaylor.ca she also had two marriages before Philip Hierlihy — Capt. John Blake (1777) and William Wishart (after 1785) — not recorded in this tree."
    ]
  }
